 🍎 Final Numbers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Financial Modeling Prep; Chart: Erin Davis/Axios Visuals Tim Cook's run as Apple CEO came to a close yesterday, 15 years after taking over for the ailing Steve Jobs.

 He didn't introduce many novel products, but supercharged the top and bottom lines as Apple became as much of a services company as a hardware company. Investors gave him high marks, with Apple shares more than doubling the Nasdaq and more than quadrupling the S&amp;P 500. Go deeper: Cook's legacy hinges on Apple's AI bets 

 
 
